## Phase 1 — Campaign State Architecture + Backend API (Week 1-2)

The Campaign State is the new first-class data structure. It orchestrates multiple assets from a single Product DNA, ensuring visual consistency across the campaign.

### Campaign State Schema
```yaml
Campaign:
  id: "campaign_001"
  product_dna: { ... }           # From the existing engine
  creative_objective: { ... }    # From OBJ-001
  creative_state: { ... }        # Solver output (renderer-agnostic)
  assets:
    - type: "hero_image"
      status: "pending | generating | complete | rejected"
      creative_state_overrides: { ... }  # Per-asset tweaks
      prompt: "..."
      image_path: null
      feedback: null
    - type: "product_closeup"
      ...
    - type: "lifestyle"
      ...
  feedback_log: []               # Track C flywheel data
  created_at: "2026-07-03T..."
  updated_at: "2026-07-03T..."
```

### Backend API Endpoints (FastAPI)
| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `/api/campaign/create` | POST | Upload product info → run engine → return Campaign State |
| `/api/campaign/{id}` | GET | Retrieve campaign with all assets |
| `/api/campaign/{id}/generate/{asset_type}` | POST | Generate a specific asset (sequential) |
| `/api/campaign/{id}/feedback` | POST | Submit approval/rejection with reason |
| `/api/campaign/{id}/export` | GET | Package all approved assets for download |

### Deliverables
- `backend/server.py` — FastAPI app wrapping the engine
- `backend/models/campaign.py` — Campaign State data model
- `backend/storage/local_store.py` — JSON file storage (hybrid path)

